## Errors: what happened and what to do

err-console-unreachable = The console does not answer.
err-unexpected = Something unexpected happened. The session is saved; please report it.
err-no-session = There is no saved session yet. Start with: ctune
err-what-now = Fix it and try again, or save and continue later.
err-bad-session = This session file cannot be read. Start a new session with: ctune
err-dev-safe-violation = Development mode: only the console emulator and the simulated hall can be used.
err-read-only-violation = The program tried to change the console while it may only read. Nothing was sent; please report it.
err-unsupported-schema = This file was written by a newer version of ChurchTune, or it is not a ChurchTune file.
err-unsafe-write = A console change was refused by the safety rules. Nothing was sent.
err-level-above-limit = The sound would be louder than the safe limit. Nothing was played.
err-audio-device = The audio device is missing or cannot run at 48 kHz. Check the USB cable from the console.
err-measurement-aborted = The sound was stopped.
err-unsupported-console = This console model is not supported by this version.
err-bad-file = A saved file of this session is damaged or missing. Your other measurements are safe.
